*.p12
*.pfx

# ── Pengyplexity runtime state (stores, workspaces, artifacts) ────────────
# Per-user data lives under PENGYPLEXITY_DATA_DIR (~/.pengyplexity by default,
# outside the repo) — these patterns catch an in-repo data dir.
#
# The moofile stores (users / memories / threads / settings / artifacts /
# shares) are the sensitive ones: users.bson holds password hashes and
# settings.bson can hold the model API key. moofile writes each as a lowercase
# `<collection>.bson` plus .cache / .lock / .meta sidecars beside it, so all of
# those forms are covered below, at any depth.
#
# Matching is case-sensitive, so the patterns use character classes to also
# catch a store that arrives from a backup or a case-insensitive filesystem
# (USERS.BSON, Users.Bson, ...).
#
# Residual gap, deliberately not papered over with speculative patterns: a store
# renamed through PENGYPLEXITY_STORE to some other extension (e.g. `store.db`)
# is NOT matched here. Keep the .bson extension, or add that path explicitly.
.pengyplexity/
*.[Bb][Ss][Oo][Nn]
*.[Bb][Ss][Oo][Nn].*
workspaces/
artifacts/

